  "description": "Bowire mock server + Mocks rail UI — ships both the mock-host runtime (MockServer, MockHandler, MockOptions, MockServerOptions) that replays Bowire recordings as a live local API endpoint (REST + gRPC unary replay, SSE / WebSocket / SignalR / MQTT streaming replay with captured frame cadence, schema-only mocks from OpenAPI / proto FileDescriptorSet / GraphQL SDL, chaos injection, stateful cursors, capture-on-miss) AND the BowireMocksRailContribution + the per-rail JS fragment the workbench stitches into its bundle. Run via `bowire mock --recording <file>`, embed with `app.UseBowireMock(...)`, or reference the package from an embedded workbench host to get the Mocks rail. The provisional Kuestenlogik.Bowire.Rail.Mocks package was folded in for v2.1.",
